// A prelude accessor's miss names its CALLER's line: `Template.part` is `@trackCaller` (KR-179). Before that it
// named the prelude (`<prelude>/global.kama:865`), and before 0.9.558 the USER's file at the prelude's line —
// `panic_location_prelude.kama:713` in a seven-line file. (`panic_location_std` holds an unmarked std body.)
fn int32 tag(Template t) { return t.part(at: 9).length() > 0 ? 1 : 0; }
fn int32 main() {
    int32 n = 1;
    return tag"a${n}b";
}
